# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is on for this checkout, which is right for most of the tree
# and wrong for anything with a shebang: a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line ending in
# CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: ... ^M". These run in CI and in
# the containers, so pin them.
*.sh text eol=lf
backend/docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Same argument, different interpreter.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
